#{[17592186442114 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186442113 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442114 #edb/ref 1069 "q-170503" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442114 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442114 #edb/ref 1071 "The minimum value of the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}-9{x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{3}^{2}-6{x}_{2}{x}_{3},$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to $-10.$ Which of the following is a vector $x$ at which the minimum is attained?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442114 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "95026062-b044-5134-829b-f9813c55ce41" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442114 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $A$ be the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form. Recall that: \n\n- The maximum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the largest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmax\\{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1\\}={\\lambda }_{\\text{max}}\n$$\n\n \nThe maximum is attained on the corresponding unit eigenvector ${u}_{\\text{max}}.$\n\n- The minimum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the smallest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmin\\{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1\\}={\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}\n$$\n\n \nThe minimum is attained on the corresponding unit eigenvector ${u}_{\\text{min}}.$\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of our quadratic form:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we need the unit eigenvector that corresponds to the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}=-10:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-(-10)I & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -9 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}+10\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}11 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-(-10)I)x=0$ gives the eigenvector $v=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$ \n\nFinally, dividing $v$ by its norm $‖v‖=\\sqrt{10},$ we get \n\n$$\n{u}_{\\text{min}}=\\frac{v}{‖v‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$